         results.push_back(soapy_device);

--
SoapySDR::Kwargs is std::map<std::string, std::string>. Assigning the int
`count` to the mapped std::string selects operator=(char), so index 0 becomes a
one-character string containing '\0' rather than "0". SoapySDR merges the
enumeration args into the args handed to makeSDDC, which does
stoul(args.at("index")) -- and stoul("\0") throws std::invalid_argument.

Observed as, with the radio present and enumerating correctly:

  ERROR novasdr_server::dsp_runner: DSP loop terminated error=open SoapySDR device
  Caused by:
      Other: stoul

This makes the driver unopenable through the normal SoapySDR::Device::make
path regardless of what the caller passes as `index`, since the enumeration
value wins the merge. Reported upstream: renardspark/SDDC_Driver.
